Package: codeep
Version: @VERSION@
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-venv, python3-pip
Recommends: python3.10, rsync
Suggests: openjdk-17-jre | default-jre, gromacs
Maintainer: Moisés Maia <moimaian@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/moimaian/CODEEP
Description: Deep-learning de novo ligand generation conditioned on the binding site
 CODEEP is a PyQt5-based graphical tool for de novo ligand design with
 deep learning: collection and curation of protein-ligand complexes,
 voxelization of the binding site into 3D tensors, hyperparameter search,
 training of a conditional variational autoencoder (3D-CNN site encoder and
 autoregressive graph-neural-network ligand decoder), evaluation, and
 generation of ranked ligand candidates, with 3D coordinates, for a new
 target protein.
 .
 This package installs the application files to /opt/codeep and a menu
 launcher. On first run, CODEEP itself creates an isolated Python virtual
 environment at ~/.venv/CODEEP and installs its own scientific dependencies
 (PyTorch, RDKit, etc.) into it, from its Install Requirements window --
 this package does not do that as root during installation, by design (see
 packaging/deb/README.md). Training data, trained models and the helper
 tools xtb and P2Rank are not part of the package; they are created or
 downloaded by the program under ~/CODEEP.
